questions.explanation:
This technical challenge evaluates expertise in multi-data center deployment, dynamic certificate lifecycle management, mutual TLS implementation, and tenant-aware routing patterns. Key assessment areas include: Vault integration for secure secrets management, Docker secrets and configs utilization, Nginx TLS configuration with mTLS enforcement, header-based tenant identification and routing, blue-green canary deployment strategies across data centers, automated bootstrap scripting, and comprehensive observability integration.

```nginx
server {
  listen 443 ssl;
  ssl_certificate /secrets/tenant.crt;
  ssl_certificate_key /secrets/tenant.key;
  ssl_client_certificate /secrets/ca.crt;
  ssl_verify_client on;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-DC data residency controls, real-time policy updates, and secure audit logging in a docker-dca setup.

## Key Concepts
- Data residency and cross-DC egress policies
- WASM-based per-tenant policy engine (Wasmtime)
- Vault-driven tenant configs and SPIFFE SVID rotation
- SIEM-based auditing and reproducible bootstrap

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo policy evaluation sketch
function evaluate(event, tenant) {
  if (event.destDC === 'DC-B' && !tenant.optIn) return 'block';
  redact(event.payload, tenant.schema);
  return 'allow';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify policy correctness across DC failover?
- How would you handle policy module hot-reload and versioning?
